user": {"login": "wenii", "id": 18167545, "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjE4MTY3NTQ1", "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/18167545?v=4", "gravatar_id": "", "url": "https://api.github.com/users/wenii", "html_url": "https://github.com/wenii", "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/wenii/followers", "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/wenii/following{/other_user}", "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/wenii/gists{/gist_id}", "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/wenii/starred{/owner}{/repo}", "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/wenii/subscriptions", "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/wenii/orgs", "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/wenii/repos", "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/wenii/events{/privacy}", "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/wenii/received_events", "type": "User", "user_view_type": "public", "site_admin": false}, "created_at": "2024-05-06T03:58:43Z", "updated_at": "2024-05-06T03:58:43Z", "body": "\r\n\"I tried both with the APM SITL simulator and a real drone. If there's no TAKE_OFF command in create_mission_raw, it won't take off. Also, keeping the TAKE_OFF command in the mission plan without explicitly calling the takeoff function won't make it take off either.\"", "author_association": "NONE", "pin": null, "reactions": {"url": "https://api.github.com/repos/mavlink/MAVSDK/issues/comments/2095155607/reactions", "total_count": 0, "+1": 0, "-1": 0, "laugh": 0, "hooray": 0, "confused": 0, "heart": 0, "rocket": 0, "eyes": 0}, "performed_via_github_app": null, "minimized": null}, {"url": "https://api.github.com/repos/mavlink/MAVSDK/issues/comments/2095160813", "html_url": "https://github.com/mavlink/MAVSDK/issues/2288#issuecomment-2095160813", "issue_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/mavlink/MAVSDK/issues/2288", "id": 2095160813, "node_id": "IC_kwDOBabE0s584Z3t", "user": {"login": "wenii", "id": 18167545, "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjE4MTY3NTQ1", "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/18167545?v=4", "gravatar_id": "", "url": "https://api.github.com/users/wenii", "html_url": "https://github.com/wenii", "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/wenii/followers", "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/wenii/following{/other_user}", "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/wenii/gists{/gist_id}", "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/wenii/starred{/owner}{/repo}", "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/wenii/subscriptions", "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/wenii/orgs", "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/wenii/repos", "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/wenii/events{/privacy}", "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/wenii/received_events", "type": "User", "user_view_type": "public", "site_admin": false}, "created_at": "2024-05-06T04:04:34Z", "updated_at": "2024-05-06T04:04:34Z", "body": "If that's the case, it's fine as long as it can take off and execute the mission. After all, the MAVSDK's compatibility with APM isn't perfect. Now, I'm facing another issue where I can't execute multiple mission plans. For instance, if I upload a mission plan and it finishes executing, then I upload another one, the second mission plan doesn't execute. There are no error reports; the drone just keeps hovering at the end of the first mission's route.", "author_association": "NONE", "pin": null, "reactions": {"url": "https://api.github.com/repos/mavlink/MAVSDK/issues/comments/2095160813/reactions", "total_count": 0, "+1": 0, "-1": 0, "laugh": 0, "hooray": 0, "confused": 0, "heart": 0, "rocket": 0, "eyes": 0}, "performed_via_github_app": null, "minimized": null}, {"url": "https://api.github.com/repos/mavlink/MAVSDK/issues/comments/2100011851", "html_url": "https://github.com/mavlink/MAVSDK/issues/2288#issuecomment-2100011851", "issue_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/mavlink/MAVSDK/issues/2288", "id": 2100011851, "node_id": "IC_kwDOBabE0s59K6NL", "user": {"login": "julianoes", "id": 1419688, "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjE0MTk2ODg=", "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1419688?v=4", "gravatar_id": "", "url": "https://api.github.com/users/julianoes", "html_url": "https://github.com/julianoes", "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/julianoes/followers", "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/julianoes/following{/other_user}", "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/julianoes/gists{/gist_id}", "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/julianoes/starred{/owner}{/repo}", "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/julianoes/subscriptions", "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/julianoes/orgs", "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/julianoes/repos", "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/julianoes/events{/privacy}", "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/julianoes/received_events", "type": "User", "user_view_type": "public", "site_admin": false}, "created_at": "2024-05-08T08:16:32Z", "updated_at": "2024-05-08T08:16:32Z", "body": "Hm, so it doesn't reset current to 0? Can you explicitly to `set_current` to reset to 0?", "author_association": "COLLABORATOR", "pin": null, "reactions": {"url": "https://api.github.com/repos/mavlink/MAVSDK/issues/comments/2100011851/reactions", "total_count": 0, "+1": 0, "-1": 0, "laugh": 0, "hooray": 0, "confused": 0, "heart": 0, "rocket": 0, "eyes": 0}, "performed_via_github_app": null, "minimized": null}, {"url": "https://api.github.com/repos/mavlink/MAVSDK/issues/comments/2100050795", "html_url": "https://github.com/mavlink/MAVSDK/issues/2288#issuecomment-2100050795", "issue_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/mavlink/MAVSDK/issues/2288", "id": 2100050795, "node_id": "IC_kwDOBabE0s59LDtr", "user": {"login": "wenii", "id": 18167545, "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjE4MTY3NTQ1", "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/18167545?v=4", "gravatar_id": "", "url": "https://api.github.com/users/wenii", "html_url": "https://github.com/wenii", "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/wenii/followers", "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/wenii/following{/other_user}", "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/wenii/gists{/gist_id}", "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/wenii/starred{/owner}{/repo}", "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/wenii/subscriptions", "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/wenii/orgs", "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/wenii/repos", "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/wenii/events{/privacy}", "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/wenii/received_events", "type": "User", "user_view_type": "public", "site_admin": false}, "created_at": "2024-05-08T08:34:15Z", "updated_at": "2024-05-08T08:34:15Z", "body": "Yes, later I found that setting set_current to 0 after uploading a new mission allows the new mission to take effect before the completion of the first mission. However, if the first mission has already been completed and a new mission is uploaded afterward, the new mission still may not execute. Then, I set the command of the last mission_item in the first mission to MAV_CMD_NAV_LOITER_UNLIM. This allows the second mission to execute seamlessly.", "author_association": "NONE", "pin": null, "reactions": {"url": "https://api.github.com/repos/mavlink/MAVSDK/issues/comments/2100050795/reactions", "total_count": 0, "+1": 0, "-1": 0, "laugh": 0, "hooray": 0, "confused": 0, "heart": 0, "rocket": 0, "eyes": 0}, "performed_via_github_app": null, "minimized": null}, {"url": "https://api.github.com/repos/mavlink/MAVSDK/issues/comments/2100079844", "html_url": "https://github.com/mavlink/MAVSDK/issues/2288#issuecomment-2100079844", "issue_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/mavlink/MAVSDK/issues/2288", "id": 2100079844, "node_id": "IC_kwDOBabE0s59LKzk", "user": {"login": "julianoes", "id": 1419688, "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjE0MTk2ODg=", "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.